{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1164","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1164","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1164\",\"parent_revision\":\"d29b35ff5ae47d68934f20470a53c7cd8cc7c659\",\"root_revision\":\"4b19c213cea0dbdf1f9e4e1232b31a29243be4c64be7a73bfe9250406dbc4140\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py script reports \\\"Successfully migrated: 0\\\" in the summary table even when 431 files were written successfully. The filesystem confirms the files exist (431 .yaml + 431 .md.bak). Observed during live migration run on 2026-03-31.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] After a successful migration run, the output clearly distinguishes \\\"0 files to migrate\\\" from \\\"migration already completed\\\"\\n- [ ] Re-running after migration shows count of existing `.yaml` and `.md.bak` files with a message like: \\\"All files appear to already be migrated (N .yaml, N .md.bak found)\\\"\\n- [ ] First-run counter still correctly reports the number of files actually migrated\\n- [ ] Tests added for `migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py`: first-run counter accuracy, re-run zero-with-messaging, error handling\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/` exits 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **migration counter bug \u2014 migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py reports 0 successfully migrated despite writing files** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 fix-append-or-replace agent migration run, 2026-03-31\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-04)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nMODIFY:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` \u2014 add state-aware messaging when `total_found == 0` and yaml/bak files exist (lines ~339\u2013379 and `_print_report` at ~479)\\n\\nCREATE:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` \u2014 new test file for the 3 scenarios above\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Fix\\n\\nAdd post-migration state detection to `run_migration` (after the glob or the migration loop):\\n\\n```python\\nyaml_count = len(list(backlog_dir.glob(\\\"*.yaml\\\")))\\nbak_count = len(list(backlog_dir.glob(\\\"*.md.bak\\\")))\\n\\nif report.total_found == 0 and yaml_count > 0:\\n    console.print(\\n        f\\\"\\\\n[yellow]No .md files to migrate \u2014 {yaml_count} .yaml files \\\"\\n        f\\\"and {bak_count} .md.bak files already exist.[/yellow]\\\"\\n    )\\n```\\n\\nThe counter logic itself does not change.\\n\\n### Missing Tests\\n\\nNo tests exist for `migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py`. `tests/test_dh_migrate.py` tests a different script (`dh_migrate.py`). Tests needed:\\n1. First run: counter matches files migrated\\n2. Re-run: counter is 0 with clear \\\"already migrated\\\" message\\n3. Error handling: files that fail round-trip verification excluded from counter\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** The counter code at `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py:369` is correct. `report.migrated += 1` executes after `migrate_file_live()` completes all 5 steps (write yaml, verify round-trip, rename .md \u2192 .md.bak). There is no code path where files are written but the counter is skipped.\\n\\n**The actual design flaw**: After a successful first run, all `.md` files become `.md.bak`. On re-run, `glob(\\\"*.md\\\")` at line 339 finds 0 files. The loop never executes. `report.migrated = 0`. The summary table correctly reports \\\"Successfully migrated: 0\\\" \u2014 but the user sees 431 `.yaml` + 431 `.md.bak` on disk and perceives a counter bug.\\n\\nThe report does not distinguish between \\\"nothing was done\\\" and \\\"everything was already done.\\\" This is a UX design flaw, not a counter bug.\\n\",\"digest\":\"e39a15f69d6ef769d6e214c8d11d3a9ce5cfc4f9a135bf45774d824bcec0a4c5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnIJEA\"}"}